there's a mystery unfolding right now in  silicon valley google's ai team has  built a chatbot that is capable of  carrying on a conversation that sounds  exactly like a human being it's uncanny  stuff and one google engineer is now  convinced that the system has gained  sentience as we interrogate his claims  i'll let you decide whether google has  solved human level artificial  intelligence or just built an elaborate  parlor trick because even if you've made  up your mind about the current state of  ai the work being done on simple  chatbots today will have staggering  consequences for the future today we are  excited to announce lambda 2 our most  advanced conversational ai with  artificial intelligence we are summoning  the demon this is a fascinating story we  have for you of a senior google engineer  who says one of the company's artificial  intelligence systems has become a  sentient being does this ai does this  bot have feelings has a.i truly become  sentient lambda  i want you to imagine a submarine  cruising through the water what word  would you use to describe that motion  the captain might say that they're  underway but only a child would say that  the submarine is swimming submarines  don't swim and yet they can travel as  fast as whales underwater asking do  machines think is a lot like asking do  submarines swim we might need to change  our frame of reference in order to find  a useful answer the question of machine  intelligence has been explored  extensively in science fiction  literature for decades but only recently  have large tech companies started  employing full-time ethicists to help  answer this question directly blake  lemoine is an engineer working for  google's responsible ai organization and  was recently tasked with testing a new  ai system called lambda it's basically  just a chat bot you ask it questions and  it types out an answer chat chatbots are  nothing new in fact one of the first  artificial intelligence demonstrations  ever 